WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Begin with the selected area and UTC window. Show the recorded satellite observations and make clear that the map is a study view, not a fire perimeter.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Show the dated activity with its unit and fixed scale. Identify any estimated or unknown dates before drawing a comparison.

3
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Show why a blank record can remain unknown. Collected exports, documented processing gaps and actual observation opportunity are different questions.

4
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Present the checked finding, then open its evidence. Keep the explanatory interpretation distinct from the saved measurement.

5
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Show an original reading and its acquisition time. Explain why a source row and an occupied common cell are different units.

6
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Close with the supported observation and the matching evidence download. Keep ignition, continuous spread, perimeter and forecast claims outside the conclusions.
